1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,737
The Power of a Growth Mindset.

2
00:00:02,687 --> 00:00:07,187
Psychologist Carol Dweck identified two fundamental mindsets.

3
00:00:07,187 --> 00:00:10,675
A fixed mindset believes intelligence is static.

4
00:00:10,675 --> 00:00:14,275
A growth mindset believes abilities can be developed.

5
00:00:14,275 --> 00:00:17,100
These beliefs become self-fulfilling.

6
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:23,350
Students taught that the brain can grow like a muscle earn higher grades and persist longer after failure.

7
00:00:23,350 --> 00:00:25,625
Mindsets are malleable.

8
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:33,850
Simply learning about neuroplasticity — the brain’s ability to form new connections throughout life — can shift how challenges are approached.

9
00:00:33,850 --> 00:00:39,200
Praising effort and strategy, not innate talent, cultivates a growth mindset.

